      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "Nice catch. One subtlety: the new check runs *after* the `nTime` refresh above it, which sets `pinfo->nTime = addr.nTime - time_penalty`. So whenever that refresh fires, the check becomes `addr.nTime - time_penalty <= addr.nTime - time_penalty` → always true → `return false`, blocking genuinely *newer* announcements too, not just re-relayed duplicates. (The existing test misses it because its `+1s` steps never trigger the refresh.)\r\n\r\nComparing against the pre-refresh value fixes it, while still blocking duplicates:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nconst NodeSeconds prev_time{pinfo->nTime};\r\n// ... existing refresh of pinfo->nTime ...\r\nif (addr.nTime - time_penalty <= prev_time) {\r\n    return false;\r\n}\r\n```",
      "user": {
        "login": "taki-abedesselam",
        "id": 25395597,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI1Mzk1NTk3",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25395597?v=4",
