      "created_at": "2026-10-16T01:51:05Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-16T01:51:05Z",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "I would like to have more clarity around when we want to attempt increasing an address' multiplicity vs when we want to simply update its timestamp. I think it would be nice to at least have some documentation around this, and the current \"do not update if no new information is present\" comment is not very explicative :)\r\n\r\nFor example, consider AddSingle being called with the following values:\r\n- `time_penalty = 2 hours`\r\n- the address is already present in our addrman, and `pinfo->nTime` is \"today at 14:30\"\r\n- `addr.nTime` is \"today at 17:00\"\r\n- `update_interval = 1 hour` (because timestamps are recent, let's say it's \"today at 18:00\" right now)\r\n\r\nThis check:\r\n```\r\nif (pinfo->nTime < addr.nTime - update_interval - time_penalty)\r\n```\r\n\r\nwould return false (\"today at 14:30\" is bigger than \"today at 17:00 minus 3h\" (\"today at 14:00\")), so we would not update the timestamp in our addrman.\r\n\r\nHowever, this check is also false:\r\n```\r\nif (addr.nTime - time_penalty <= pinfo->nTime) {\r\n```\r\n(\"today at 17:00 minus 2h\" is bigger than \"today at 14:30\"). So we would not return from the function, and go on and attempt increasing the multiplicity of the address in the addrman.\r\n",
      "user": {
        "login": "danielabrozzoni",
        "id": 25042473,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDQyNDcz",
